h  they're not happy about having the  attack on Mars take place on April 5th  marks a sharp parallel to the day's  original theme of interspecies  cooperation and Trust following the  attack the Federation would abandon  their attempt to save the Romulan people  and would also ban synthetics entirely  when Picard's doctor comes to visit him  in maps and legends he brings with him  the somber news that he suspects that a  small defect in Picard's parietal lobe  may have triggered  of several related neurological  syndromes the two of them talked about  the defect itself as though the  knowledge of it is old news which it is  the defect was first discovered by dr.  Beverly Crusher in the next-generation  series finale all good things that  episode saw Picard's skipping through  time including one thread in the distant  future when he learns that he will  eventually develop a rheumatic syndrome  a degenerative neurological condition  that can cause confusion hallucinations  and paranoia the card has crusher scan  him in his present timeline for possible  warning signs and while she finds no  traces of the syndrome she does notice a  small defect in the parietal lobe which  could but won't necessarily eventually  lead to Ihram addict syndrome while  neither Picard nor his doctor mentioned  aromatic syndrome by name and maps and  legends it's clear that this is what  Picard is worried about in all good  things we see that the future older  Picard is often second-guessed and  discounted due to his diagnosis leading  to him going against the orders of  Starfleet and calling in favors to  obtain a ship and carry out his mission  a plotline that seems like it may be  rearing its head once again when Picard  steps into the lobby of Starfleet  headquarters a voice can be heard over  the intercom paging a certain Admiral  although it's easy to dismiss this line  a simple background chatter the name  gurney has some surprising significance  in the 1984 science fiction film dune